   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 434 of the laws of 2022 authorizing the commissioner\nof the office of general services to convey certain unappropriated state land\nto KIPP: Albany Community Public Charter Schools, in relation to the time of\ntransfer of certain lands and to the effectiveness of such provisions",
    "basePrintNo": "S8041",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8041-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§4 & 6, Chap 434 of 2022",
    "lawSection": "Public Lands",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8041\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 434 of the laws of 2022 authorizing the commis-\nsioner of the office of general services to convey certain unappropri-\nated state land to KIPP: Albany Community Public Charter Schools, in\nrelation to the time of transfer of certain lands and to the effective-\nness of such provisions\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nProvides the authorization to the Commissioner of General Services to\ntransfer and convey the state-owned land located at 596 Manning Boule-\nvard, Albany, New York to KIPP Capital Region Public Charter Schools.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1:  Provides  authorization  for  the  Commissioner of OGS to\ntransfer and convey such lands to KIPP  Capital  Region  Public  Charter\nSchools, upon terms and conditions deemed proper.\n\n  Section  2:  Provides  general  description  of  the  state-owned land\nlocated at 596 Manning Boulevard, Albany, New York that the Commissioner\nof OGS is authorized to transfer and convey.\n\n  Section 3: Provides that the description of the land in section two of\nthis bill is not meant to be a legal description, and that, as a  condi-\ntion of any conveyance, KIPP Capital Region Public Charter Schools shall\nsubmit  to the Commissioner of OGS a survey and description of the prop-\nerty.\n\n  Section 4: Provides that the Commissioner of OGS  shall  transfer  and\nconvey  the  property  described  in  section  two of this act only upon\napplication by KIPP Capital Region Public Charter  Schools,  provides  a\ntimeline for the application and conveyance.\n\n  Section  5:  Provides  for the approved uses of the land and that upon\ntermination of such use the land shall revert to the State of New York.\n\n  Section 6: Provides for an immediate effective date that shall  expire\nafter three years of such date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe  land  located at 596 Manning Boulevard, Albany, New York, is vacant\nproperty owned by the People of the State of New  York,  acting  by  and\nthrough  the Commissioner of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation\nof the State of New York. The transfer of this property  will  alleviate\nthe need for maintenance and liability costs to the State and allow KIPP\nCapital  Region Public Charter Schools to maintain the property, improve\ntraffic flow,  and  provide  increased  public  access  to  Tivoli  Lake\nPreserve in conjunction with the City of Albany.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT:\n\nTo be determined.   \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately,  and  shall expire and be deemed repealed three years after\nsuch date.\n",
